      do not invent false knowledge semantics or restore a parallel complete/supplemental model.
    ☑ Preserve existing stable bit assignments and public invalidation groups. Choose enum widths
      that fit every defined bit; avoid narrowing a shared knowledge enum to fit only its value subset.
    ☑ Replace redundant boolean backing fields with flags. Preserve useful named boolean properties
      as accessors where this keeps call sites clear; those properties must have no separate storage.
      Use Enum.HasFlag for reads and typed bitwise OR/AND-complement for setting/clearing bits.
    ☑ Preserve default values, constructor/object-initializer behavior, tuple/group semantics,
      equality and hash behavior where applicable, and independently owned indexed payloads.
